# PromiseOne – System Rules (not in use currently)

This file defines non-negotiable rules for working on PromiseOne.
Any human or AI helper must read this before making changes.

---

## 1. Execution Context

- All PowerShell commands assume execution from:
  C:\PromiseOne\core
- If not already there, the first command must be:
  cd C:\PromiseOne\core

---

## 2. PowerShell Input Rules

- Raw JSON or object literals are NEVER pasted directly into PowerShell
- Structured content must use ONE of:
  - Here-strings (@' '@) with Set-Content
  - A dedicated .ps1 script file
- If PowerShell errors with:
  "'{' is not recognized as an internal or external command"
  then the input format is invalid

---

## 3. Copy–Paste Safety

- All instructions must be safe to paste as a single block
- Line-by-line execution is NOT allowed unless explicitly stated
- If a block must be split, that must be clearly labeled

---

## 4. Content Library Rules

- All reusable content lives under:
  content/library
- One concept per JSON file
- No hardcoded content inside templates
- Templates reference content; content never references templates

---

## 5. File Creation Rules

- Directories must be created before writing files
- Use:
  mkdir <path> -Force
- Use:
  Set-Content (not Out-File unless encoding matters)

---

## 6. Error Handling Protocol

- Red text is informational, not emotional
- First question is always:
  “What did PowerShell interpret this input as?”
- No guessing, no retrying blindly

---

## 7. Engine Design Philosophy

- Deterministic > clever
- Explicit > implicit
- If behavior is unclear, it is considered a bug

---

## 8. Continuity Rule

- Any helper must follow these rules exactly
- If a suggestion violates a rule, it must be flagged before execution
